        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1352556795,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "Native Americans used fiber in the stems for rope, basketry, and nets. Some Native Americans used the milky sap for medicinal purposes.\nAlthough care is needed to distinguish the species from highly toxic species in the genus, the young leaves and seed pods of A. speciosa can be boiled and eaten.",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "es": {
